[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug: the parser reads dates month first. Its own table
says otherwise. Read the reports, not the subject lines, and #4471 holds three problems with
three different fixes. Queuing the parser fix closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not known. Two of its problems had no ticket until this page. Each now has its own.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

### `parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first

A day-first tenant books 7 June; the invite says 6 July. It hits every tenant and every channel
(app, email and form). This is the bug #4471 names, and the fix that is queued.

### `hint`: booking-v3's form tells people to type month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People do what the hint says, then the form
reads their date the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix does not touch this: the hint and
the form disagree with each other. Only reports that came in through the form of a booking-v3
tenant (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) belong here. The fix is the hint, not the parser.

### `shift`: dates move by one day

These reports are not a flip. "Tuesday 12 May, calendar says Monday 11 May". "Client in Lisbon
got Tuesday, client in Toronto got Monday". "Every booking in June is one day off". A day and a
month that trade places cannot do that. It points at time zones or a daylight-saving boundary,
not at date order. The desk saw it (`desk-notes.json`, "one-day move") and still filed these
under the parser, by tenant.

## Why they were merged

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone, and every
  one of these reports says some version of "wrong day". Same words, different bugs.
- Intake's tag comes from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant: every report tagged `hint`
  came from an `en-US` browser. Tag and cause disagree in both directions (see below). Do not
  triage by the tag.

## The desk's own view

The table the incident page already renders. It splits `hint` out but counts `shift` under
`parser` and leaves it in a footnote.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What changes on the desk

- Close #4471 against `parser` only. Reopen nothing; track `hint` and `shift` in their own tickets.
- When a report's body does not match the ticket's bug, split it out, even when the subject matches.
- Decision 0001 needs a successor record: same subject is a hint to read, not a reason to merge.

